---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ReviewCard from '../components/ReviewCard.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import FinalCta from '../components/FinalCta.astro';
import { SITE, PENDING, estherMonths } from '../data/site';
import { REVIEWS } from '../data/content';
import { breadcrumb, person } from '../data/schema';
const months = estherMonths();
const crumbs = [{ name: 'About', path: '/about' }];
const rules = [
  ['shield-check', 'Pre-confirm everything', 'No product ships without a creator confirmation. No guarantee goes unwritten.'],
  ['target', 'Volume isn’t optional', 'Every plan has a guaranteed post count. We report posts against target first, every month.'],
  ['handshake', 'You own everything', 'Every creator contact, content link and the tracker stay yours, even if you leave.'],
  ['layers', 'Category depth', 'Beauty only. That’s why the Competitor Creator Audit is accurate.'],
  ['eye', 'Transparency is the deliverable', 'A live tracker from day one. You verify, you don’t trust blindly.']
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Influencer Orbit · Creator Seeding for Beauty"
  description="Not an influencer agency. A confirm-first creator seeding operation built only for DTC beauty brands, founded by Tayyab Habib."
  path="/about"
  schema={[breadcrumb(crumbs), person()]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
      <p class="eyebrow">About Influencer Orbit</p>
      <h1 class="h-hero">Not an influencer agency. <em>A creator seeding operation.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">Agencies sell campaigns. Marketplaces sell access to a creator pool. Software sells a dashboard someone still has to run. We run the operation: guaranteed creator posts every month for DTC beauty brands, with the best ones turned into ads.</p>
      <div class="chipline"><span><Icon name="users" />4-person team</span><span><Icon name="globe" />Fully remote</span><span><Icon name="clock" />Reply within one business day</span><span><Icon name="star" /><span data-months>{months}</span> months with one beauty brand</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight" aria-labelledby="pov-title">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHead id="pov-title" eyebrow="Our point of view" title="Creator seeding isn’t broken. <em>Sending product and hoping is.</em>" />
      <div class="split">
        <div class="prose" style="margin:0">
          <p>Most brands run gifting like this: find some creators, ship boxes, wait. Then 30% to 50% of them post (<a href="https://blog.hypeauditor.com/how-to-get-influencers-to-post-about-your-brand-during-a-gifting-campaign/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HypeAuditor</a>), and someone loses a week chasing the rest.</p>
          <p>We saw that pattern over and over and asked why. The answer was structural. Nobody confirmed before shipping, and nobody followed up until the post was live.</p>
          <p>So we built the operation around one rule: <strong>no creator gets product until they confirm.</strong> Everything else we do, from the audit to the tracker to the VIP roster, sits on top of that rule.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="band on-dark" style="text-align:left;padding:40px">
          <p class="h-lg" style="color:#fff;margin:0">“The brands that win creator distribution aren’t the ones with the biggest budgets. They’re the ones with the <em>most disciplined operations</em>.”</p>
          <p style="margin:20px 0 0;max-width:none">Tayyab Habib, Founder</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <div class="container founder">
      <div class="founder__photo">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/images/brand/tayyab-habib-480.avif 480w, /images/brand/tayyab-habib-800.avif 800w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 420px, 90vw" />
          <img src="/images/brand/tayyab-habib-800.webp" srcset="/images/brand/tayyab-habib-480.webp 480w, /images/brand/tayyab-habib-800.webp 800w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 420px, 90vw" width="800" height="800" alt="Tayyab Habib, founder of Influencer Orbit" loading="lazy" />
        </picture>
        <div class="founder__badge"><img src="/images/brand/app-icon-192.png" width="36" height="36" alt="" /><div><b>{SITE.founder.name}</b>Founder, Influencer Orbit</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="founder__text">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
        <h2 id="story-title" class="h-xl">Built from <em>execution</em>, not a pitch deck.</h2>
        {PENDING.founderStory && <p class="mt-6">{PENDING.founderStory}</p>}
        <p class="mt-6">In January 2024, Esther Formula, a Korean skincare and beauty supplement brand, needed 50 to 200 creator posts a month. That’s more than their team could reach while also running the business. We built the confirm-first system for them, and it’s still running <span data-months>{months}</span> months later: 2,000+ creator collaborations, 200+ shipments coordinated a month, and no in-house influencer manager ever hired.</p>
        <p>We chose to go deep with one brand instead of touching dozens once. That depth is why we know which creators have real skincare audiences, which hooks work for retinol versus glutathione, and which claims get content pulled.</p>
        <p class="mt-6"><a class="text-link" href={SITE.founder.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Connect with Tayyab on LinkedIn <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="rules-title">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHead id="rules-title" eyebrow="How we operate" title="Five rules <em>we run on</em>." />
      <div class="grid grid--3">
        {rules.map(([icon, title, text]) => (
          <div class="card card--hover reveal"><span class="icon-dot"><Icon name={icon} /></span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div>
        ))}
        <div class="card card--soft reveal" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0">Category depth over breadth</h3>
          <p>We work only with DTC skincare, cosmetics and beauty brands, and source creators wherever your customers are: the US, Southeast Asia, the UK, Australia and the UAE.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="team-title">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHead id="team-title" eyebrow="The team" title="A four-person operations team, <em>built for volume</em>." lead="Tayyab handles strategy and every client conversation. The team runs creator research, outreach, shipping coordination and post tracking. We’re fully remote, based in Pakistan, with a live tracker you can check any time and a one-business-day response commitment written into every engagement." />
      <div class="compare-wrap" style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="team-title">
        <table class="compare" style="min-width:520px">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Others sell</th><th scope="col" class="is-us">We run</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>One campaign, one invoice</td><td class="is-us"><span class="mark mark--yes"><Icon name="check" />A monthly seeding operation that compounds</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reach and “estimated impressions”</td><td class="is-us"><span class="mark mark--yes"><Icon name="check" />Posts against target, in writing</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Their creator pool</td><td class="is-us"><span class="mark mark--yes"><Icon name="check" />Creators hand-vetted for your customer</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Relationships they keep</td><td class="is-us"><span class="mark mark--yes"><Icon name="check" />A roster and tracker you keep</span></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="reviews-title">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHead id="reviews-title" eyebrow="Reviews" title="On time, easy to work with, <em>worth hiring again</em>." lead="Verified reviews from clients Tayyab has worked with, quoted word for word." />
      <div class="reviews" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Client reviews">
        {REVIEWS.map((r) => <ReviewCard {...r} />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FinalCta
    title="See the operation running <em>before you decide</em>."
    micro="We’ll show you the live Esther Formula tracker and the report you’d receive."
    secondary={false}
  />
</BaseLayout>
